# Documentation SDLC (always)

This repo prototypes a **Cursor-driven SDLC**. Agents own documentation quality; do not rely on CI doc gates or human PR checklists.

## Before every commit / push / PR

1. Read [planning/DOC-MAP.md](../../planning/DOC-MAP.md) and classify the change.
2. Update every doc listed for that change type **in the same branch** as the code.
3. Run skill **`/sync-documentation`** before opening or updating a PR.
4. For dependency expansion (profiles, packages, effect patterns, dogfood): run **`/ship-dependency-feature`** instead of or in addition to sync-documentation.

## Non-negotiables

- **Ship status** changes (feature complete, backlog reorder) → update doc 15 strike-through grid, doc 09 priorities, and README when user-facing.
- **Never** leave planning docs listing shipped work as "next" (see subtype lords / tokens / vehicles pattern in doc 15).
- If no docs need updates, state why explicitly in the PR body.

## PR body

Include a **Documentation** section listing touched files or "none — [reason]". See DOC-MAP PR template.
